    Therefore, there are \(\binom{p}{j}\) distinct ways to orient this outer product and for \(\binom{p-1}{j-1}\) of them the vector \(\vek{s}\) is applied to the \(j\)-tensor and for \(\binom{p-1}{j}\) to the \((p-j)\)-tensor.
